# Normalise line endings in the repository, not just in the working tree.
#
# Found by CLONING this repository and running the suite on the clone: it failed.
#
#   CALLBACKS.md is out of date. Run: node tools/gen-docs.js
#
# Nothing was out of date. `npm run test:docs` compares the committed file
# against freshly generated output byte for byte, and a Windows checkout with
# core.autocrlf=true hands it CRLF while the generator writes LF. The check
# reports "stale" on a tree where nothing is stale.
#
# That is not cosmetic. A check that fails on a byte git itself considers
# insignificant is a check people disable -- and then it stops catching the
# drift it exists to catch, which is the exact failure it was written to
# prevent. A generated-file gate that cries wolf is worse than no gate.
#
# `* text=auto eol=lf` makes LF the form in the repository AND in the working
# tree on every platform, so generated output is byte-comparable everywhere.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets must never be line-ending translated.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.zip binary
*.pdf binary
*.lua.bak binary
